WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.208
Entry-to-practice readiness is not a memorized script. It is the ability to collect relevant evidence, identify what cannot wait, choose a safe action, evaluate the response and explain the next step without depending on a prompt.
入职执业准备度不是背熟一套脚本，而是能收集相关证据、识别不能等待的问题、选择安全行动、评价反应，并在没有提示时说明下一步。

00:00:14.208 --> 00:00:29.592
Use the school’s A01–A04 review as four connected lenses: clinical approach, patient assessment, communication and transfer, and duty of care. The actual current guideline and your licence determine what you may do.
把学校指定复习的A01–A04作为四个相连视角：临床处置方法、患者评估、沟通与交接、照护责任。实际可做什么由现行指南和个人执照决定。

00:00:29.592 --> 00:00:51.384
The saved Week Fourteen plan names A one through A four, the eye, ear, nose and throat cases, a five-minute patient care record practice and a zero-feedback lab standard. The detailed lab guide was not yet available in our course check. This lesson prepares the published objectives; it does not reproduce that unseen guide.
保存的第十四周计划列出A01至A04、眼耳鼻喉案例、五分钟PCR练习及零反馈实验标准。核对当前课程时，详细实验指南仍未开放。本课准备学校已公布的目标，不声称复现尚未看到的指南。

00:00:51.384 --> 00:01:12.984
One local BCPEG copy contains 94 PDF pages. Its physical page 80 contains general practical-examination deficiency categories; the assigned pages 274–276 are outside that copy. Keep that mismatch visible and do not invent the missing criteria.
本地一份BCPEG文件共94个PDF物理页。其物理第80页包含实操考试通用缺陷分类；指定的274–276页超出该文件范围。必须保留这一差异，不得编造缺失标准。

00:01:12.984 --> 00:01:28.296
The school plan says the Week 14 lab begins a “Zero Feedback” standard. For preparation, treat this as a no-hint performance run: the learner must state the concern, plan and reassessment without coaching during the scenario.
学校计划表示第14周实验开始采用“零反馈”标准。备课时可把它理解为无提示表现：学习者须在情景中自行说出问题、计划和复评，不由教官提示。

00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:46.512
This is an original practice interpretation, not a verified official lab rubric. Zero prompts do not require an instructor to allow imminent harm. Safety control stays active; teaching feedback can be held until the run ends, then tied to observable evidence.
这是原创练习解释，并非经核实的官方实验评分表。零提示不要求教官放任即将发生的伤害；安全控制仍须有效。教学反馈可以留到情景结束后，再依据可观察证据讨论。

00:01:46.512 --> 00:02:00.048
An original practice case: a six-year-old has fever, new drooling and laboured breathing. The child leans forward with the hands braced on the knees and becomes more distressed when asked to lie back.
原创练习案例：一名六岁儿童发热、新出现流涎和费力呼吸。孩子前倾、双手支撑膝部；被要求躺下时呼吸窘迫加重。

00:02:00.048 --> 00:02:20.928
What matters first is the pattern and trajectory, not proving a label. Drooling, swallowing difficulty, respiratory distress and a preferred upright posture raise concern for a critical upper-airway problem. Keep the child with a caregiver if helpful, minimize agitation and prepare early escalation.
首先要看的是表现组合和变化趋势，而不是证明某个诊断。流涎、吞咽困难、呼吸窘迫和偏好直立体位提示可能存在危重上气道问题。若有帮助，可让孩子靠近照护者，尽量减少刺激，并及早准备升级处置。

00:02:20.928 --> 00:02:37.512
BCEHS B04 describes pediatric epiglottitis as often abrupt, with drooling, dysphagia and distressed breathing; tripod positioning and reluctance to lie down are classic warning signs. Cough may be absent or uncommon.
BCEHS B04指出，儿童会厌炎常为突然起病，表现为流涎、吞咽困难和呼吸窘迫；三脚架体位及不愿躺下是典型警示表现。咳嗽可能缺如或并不常见。

00:02:37.512 --> 00:02:57.576
A peritonsillar or other deep-neck infection can also produce painful swallowing, altered voice or airway concern. Do not force a comparison by making the child open the mouth. Keep the working description at the level supported by observation: “possible critical upper-airway infection or obstruction.”
扁桃体周围或其他深颈部感染也可能导致吞咽疼痛、声音改变或气道风险。不要要求孩子张口来强行鉴别。工作描述应停留在观察证据支持的层面，例如“可能的危重上气道感染或梗阻”。

00:02:57.576 --> 00:03:14.832
For suspected epiglottitis, BCEHS B04 says not to attempt to visualize the oropharynx unless airway control is necessary in a severely decompensated patient. An unneeded throat examination can worsen distress and risk sudden deterioration.
疑似会厌炎时，BCEHS B04要求不要试图观察口咽，除非患者严重失代偿且为了控制气道确有必要。无必要的咽喉检查可能加重窘迫，并带来突然恶化的风险。

00:03:14.832 --> 00:03:33.504
Use information you can obtain without provoking the child: position of comfort, ability to speak or swallow, breathing effort, colour, level of responsiveness, onset, fever history and relevant collateral information. Do not delay urgent transport planning for a complete interview.
使用无需刺激患儿即可取得的信息：舒适体位、说话或吞咽能力、呼吸做功、肤色、反应水平、起病情况、发热史和相关旁证。不要为了完成整套问诊而延误紧急转运计划。

00:03:33.504 --> 00:03:50.232
The immediate objective is to avoid worsening a precarious airway while arranging definitive care. Keep the child calm and in the position they choose, obtain essential observations without delay, and mobilize the transport and support plan early.
当前目标是在安排进一步救治的同时避免恶化脆弱气道。让孩子保持平静并维持其选择的体位，及时获得必要观察，并尽早启动转运和支援计划。

00:03:50.232 --> 00:04:10.776
Monitor continuously for change. A quieter child is not necessarily improving: declining interaction, reduced effort from fatigue, colour change or worsening air movement can represent deterioration. Follow the current pathway and local scope; this lesson does not authorize an airway procedure.
持续监测变化。孩子安静下来不一定表示好转：互动减少、因疲劳而呼吸做功下降、肤色改变或气流进一步减弱都可能表示恶化。应遵循现行流程和本地执业范围；本课不授权任何气道操作。

00:04:10.776 --> 00:04:26.544
A second original case: while diluting a concentrated cleaning product, an adult receives a splash to one eye. A coworker can identify the product container, but the eyewash saline bag is still being fetched and clean running water is available.
第二个原创案例：一名成人稀释浓缩清洁剂时，一只眼睛被溅到。工友能指出产品容器，但眼部冲洗用盐水仍在取来途中，现场有清洁流动水。

00:04:26.544 --> 00:04:43.320
First control the scene and protect yourself from secondary exposure. Do not enter an unsafe contamination area. Ask a partner to obtain the product label or safety sheet while irrigation begins; the patient must not wait for paperwork or an ideal solution.
首先控制现场并防止自己受到二次暴露。不要进入不安全的污染区域。可让同伴获取产品标签或安全资料，同时开始冲洗；不能让患者为了等文件或理想冲洗液而等待。

00:04:43.320 --> 00:05:04.656
BCEHS H04 calls for starting normal-saline irrigation for a chemical eye injury while attempting to identify the substance. BCEHS J01 also directs flushing an exposed eye with water. If clean water is available and saline is not yet present, do not leave the eye exposed while waiting for saline.
BCEHS H04要求化学眼伤在尝试识别化学物质的同时开始生理盐水冲洗。BCEHS J01也要求眼部暴露后用水冲洗。如果现场有清洁水而盐水尚未到位，不要让眼睛继续暴露，只为等待盐水。

00:05:04.656 --> 00:05:24.072
Use a controlled gentle flow and direct runoff away from the uninjured eye and the responder. Remove a contact lens only if it is loose and can be removed without delaying irrigation or causing additional injury. Follow current hazardous-material controls and required chemical-exposure consultation.
使用可控、轻柔的水流，并让流出液远离未受伤眼和救援人员。只有当隐形眼镜松动且取出不会延误冲洗或造成额外伤害时才移除。遵循现行危害物控制要求，并进行规定的化学暴露咨询。

00:05:24.072 --> 00:05:43.392
The school scenario specifies normal-saline irrigation for a minimum of 15 minutes before other assessment. Learn that wording for the school exercise. Separately, current BCEHS guidance says to start irrigation, contact CliniCall for chemical-exposure support, and follow the chemical-specific plan.
学校情景规定先用生理盐水冲洗至少15分钟，再进行其他评估。学校练习中要记住这项表述。另一方面，BCEHS现行指导要求开始冲洗、联系CliniCall获取化学暴露支持，并遵循具体化学物质的处置方案。

00:05:43.392 --> 00:06:04.680
The 15-minute school timer is not a universal stop rule. If saline is unavailable, suitable clean water is better than delaying. At the 15-minute mark, do not automatically stop if symptoms, product properties or consultation indicate continued irrigation; reassess and follow current instructions.
学校的15分钟计时不是通用的停止规则。如果暂时没有盐水，适当的清洁水胜过延误。在15分钟时，如果症状、产品特性或咨询意见提示应继续冲洗，不要自动停止；应复评并遵循现行指示。

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:19.848
For a suspected penetrating object, leave it in place and stabilize it as appropriate. Do not press on the globe, attempt removal, or use a tight dressing. A rigid shield can protect the eye while avoiding direct contact.
怀疑有穿透物时，应保留原位并适当固定。不要压迫眼球、尝试拔除或使用紧压敷料。可用硬质护罩保护眼睛，同时避免直接接触。

00:06:19.848 --> 00:06:38.304
BCEHS H04 emphasizes avoiding pressure, leaving penetrating objects in place, prompt conveyance and not delaying treatment or transport for visual-acuity testing. Consider associated head injury and other trauma from the same mechanism; use current trauma guidance.
BCEHS H04强调避免施压、保留穿透物、及时转运，并且不能为了测视力而延误治疗或转运。还要考虑同一机制造成的头部伤及其他创伤，并遵循现行创伤指导。

00:06:38.304 --> 00:06:52.608
BCEHS E11 recommends sitting upright and leaning slightly forward, then compressing the nose bilaterally just distal to the bridge for at least 15 minutes. The patient should not tilt the head back or repeatedly release pressure to check.
BCEHS E11建议患者坐直并略微前倾，然后在鼻梁下方偏远端压住双侧鼻翼至少15分钟。患者不应后仰头部，也不应反复松手查看。

00:06:52.608 --> 00:07:12.456
Keep assessing the whole patient. Ask about trauma, anticoagulant or antiplatelet medicines, bleeding disorders and relevant medical history. Ongoing bleeding, risk factors or deterioration require escalation under current guidance; paramedics should not generally pack the nares.
继续评估患者整体状况。询问创伤、抗凝或抗血小板药物、出血性疾病和相关病史。持续出血、危险因素或病情恶化时，应按现行指导升级处置；急救人员通常不应自行填塞鼻腔。

00:07:12.456 --> 00:07:31.896
Physical page 80 of the saved June 2026 BCPEG snapshot describes major, moderate and minor practical-examination deficiencies. It emphasizes whether an indicated task was done, whether the sequence was safe, and whether critical information was included in the record or report.
保存的2026年6月版BCPEG物理第80页描述了实操考试中的重大、中度和轻微缺陷。它强调是否完成必要任务、顺序是否安全，以及记录或报告中是否包含关键信息。

00:07:31.896 --> 00:07:53.736
Use those categories to notice risk and sequence errors, but do not invent a W14-specific official checklist or predict a pass result from this course. The same saved file does not contain assigned pages 274–276. Follow the actual school-issued exam criteria when available.
可用这些分类识别风险和顺序错误，但不要编造第14周专用的官方清单，也不要根据本课程预测考试是否通过。同一保存文件中并无指定的274–276页。实际考试标准开放后，应以学校发布的版本为准。

00:07:53.736 --> 00:08:10.080
The school plan names a five-minute PCR target for practice. Treat the clock as a preparation tool: make the record organized and efficient, but never invent a finding or omit a legally or operationally required detail merely to beat the timer.
学校计划规定了五分钟PCR练习目标。应把计时视为组织训练：记录要有条理且高效，但绝不能为了赶时间而捏造发现，或省略法律或操作要求的信息。

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:28.560
Before writing, make a short timeline and identify the facts that change care: onset, objective observations, change over time, actions, response, consultation and unresolved risk. Use the service record and the actual rubric for required fields.
写记录前先列出简短时间线，找出会改变照护决策的事实：起病、客观观察、时间趋势、采取的行动、反应、咨询及未解决风险。必填字段以服务记录系统和实际评分表为准。

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:51.144
Give a concise oral handover and a separate accurate PCR. For the child, communicate the airway threat, posture, distress, change and any examination intentionally avoided. For the eye exposure, communicate the chemical identity if known, irrigation start and duration, fluid used and consultation plan.
口头交接要简明，PCR则单独完整准确。儿童案例中，应交代上气道风险、体位、窘迫、变化，以及有意避免的检查。眼部暴露案例中，应交代已知的化学物质、冲洗开始时间和时长、使用液体及咨询计划。

00:08:51.144 --> 00:09:06.264
Use the school’s assigned handover format during its station, and use the current service format in actual practice. Confirm that the receiver understands the immediate risk and next step; do not assume a message was received without acknowledgment.
学校站点练习时使用指定交接格式，实际工作中使用现行服务格式。确认接收者理解即时风险和下一步；没有明确回应时，不要假设信息已被接收。

00:09:06.264 --> 00:09:36.072
Return to the eye-exposure station. Before reaching for a probe, bottle or tablet, map the patient threat and the clean and dirty tasks. Infection precautions and chemical protection are related but not identical. Select the actual compatible barriers, prepare supplies and contain runoff without spreading contamination. Give your partner a clear role while the necessary initial care proceeds; wearing gloves is not the whole safety plan.
回到化学溅眼站。在触碰探头、冲洗瓶或平板电脑前，先判断患者面临的威胁，并划分清洁与污染操作。感染预防与化学防护有关联，但不是同一回事。选择与实际危险相匹配的防护用品，备好物资，控制流出液，避免污染扩散。必要的初始照护应持续进行，同时明确同伴的任务；戴上手套并不等于完成安全计划。

00:09:36.072 --> 00:10:05.736
The assigned CPSC range explains how transmission is interrupted at several links. Hands, equipment, clothing and the documentation device can each carry contamination. A clean hand becomes contaminated again on a dirty control. Arrange the sequence so the person maintaining irrigation does not pass dirty gloves to the radio or the next patient. If an exposure occurs, use appropriate first aid and reporting rather than concealing it to keep a station score.
指定的CPSC阅读解释如何在多个环节阻断传播。手、设备、衣物和记录设备都可能携带污染物；清洁的手触碰污染控制键后，也会再次受污染。安排好操作顺序，避免负责冲洗的人戴着污染手套触碰无线电或下一位患者。若发生暴露，应进行适当急救并按流程报告，不能为了保住站点评分而隐瞒。

00:10:05.736 --> 00:10:35.808
The two VSM pages connect consent, privacy and infection prevention. Introduce the proposed measurement and obtain the appropriate permission, but keep urgent care moving. For hand hygiene, learn what the time refers to. Fifteen-second soap friction is still described in selected healthcare guidance; a whole handwash procedure includes wetting, rinsing and drying as well. A different number does not automatically mean the textbook is obsolete.
VSM这两页把同意、隐私和感染预防联系起来。应解释拟进行的测量并获得适当同意，同时不延误紧急照护。学习手卫生计时时，要先弄清计时涵盖什么：部分医疗指导仍描述约十五秒的肥皂揉搓，而完整洗手还包括湿手、冲洗和擦干。不同数字不一定互相矛盾，也不能直接证明教材过时。

00:10:35.808 --> 00:11:04.296
Use the actual approved product and local procedure, clean all relevant hand surfaces and allow drying before gloves. Reassess visible soil and specific precautions when choosing hand rub or soap and water. Gloves never replace hand hygiene, and cleaning your hands never replaces cleaning a contaminated cuff or probe. Explain that chain during debrief instead of presenting a single timer as proof that the process was safe.
使用机构批准的产品及本地流程，清洁所有相关手部表面，干燥后再戴手套。选择手消毒剂还是肥皂和水时，应考虑可见污物及特定防护要求。手套不能替代手卫生，清洁双手也不能替代清洁受污染的袖带或探头。复盘时应解释整个污染控制链，不能只凭一个计时数字宣称过程安全。

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:31.824
The PHARM review covers the full safety and administration chain, not a new drug list. Check the patient and indication, real authorization, formulation, previous doses, allergies and relevant interactions before calculation. Then verify route, equipment and monitoring. A correct number does not make the wrong product or an unneeded treatment safe, and access to a vein or tube does not prove compatibility.
PHARM复习涵盖完整的用药安全与给药流程，不是一份新增药物清单。计算前，核实患者、指征、实际授权、剂型、既往剂量、过敏及相关相互作用，再检查途径、器材和监测。数字算对，不能让错误产品或不必要的治疗变安全；已有静脉或管路，也不能证明药物与该途径兼容。

00:11:31.824 --> 00:12:02.496
For an arithmetic simulation only, a training label says six milligrams in three milliliters and the simulated amount is three milligrams. Concentration is two milligrams per milliliter, so the calculated volume is one point five milliliters. Reverse-check the multiplication. No medicine or patient indication is supplied by that example. In the actual station, resolve a discrepancy while maintaining appropriate support rather than guessing to avoid a pause.
以下仅作算术模拟：训练标签为三毫升含六毫克，模拟所需量为三毫克。浓度是每毫升二毫克，因此体积为一点五毫升，再用乘法反向核算。这个例子没有指定任何真实药物或患者指征。实际站点遇到差异，应在维持适当支持的同时澄清，不能为了避免暂停而猜测。

00:12:02.496 --> 00:12:31.104
A one and A two organize continuous assessment: changing scene risk, a first impression, immediate threats, relevant history and focused examination. Address the threat when found and make meaningful use of the partner. Do not inspect a potentially fragile child airway just to complete a physical examination, or stop necessary eye irrigation to obtain a routine score. The depth and sequence follow the actual patient.
A01与A02组织的是持续评估：动态现场风险、第一印象、即时威胁、相关病史和聚焦检查。发现威胁就应处理，并合理利用同伴。不能只为完成体检而检查可能脆弱的儿童气道，也不能为取得常规评分而停止必要的眼部冲洗。评估深度与顺序应由真实患者需要决定。

00:12:31.104 --> 00:13:01.344
The source deterioration charts are supporting tools. One severely abnormal component matters, and an incomplete set must not be called normal. The child requires an age-appropriate approach, not an adult score. Also keep the source COPD shortcut distinct from the original scoring guidance: choosing an oxygen-saturation scale is not the same decision as prescribing oxygen. A low total cannot clear a serious local injury or erase a concerning change.
来源中的恶化评分只是辅助工具。单项严重异常仍然重要，数据不完整不能称作正常。儿童需要适龄方法，而非成人评分。还应区分来源中针对COPD的简化说法与原始评分指导：选择血氧评分量表，不等于决定氧疗处方。低总分不能排除严重局部损伤，也不能抹去令人担忧的变化。

00:13:01.344 --> 00:13:30.096
A four carries responsibility through the encounter. Anticipate what care may be needed, match the receiving team to that need and resolve a mismatch. A source fifteen-minute interval, one normal vital-sign set or arrival at the hospital does not complete the transfer. Consolidated care also needs explicit roles, equipment, monitoring and a response to deterioration; a patient count is not a universal staffing rule.
A04强调照护责任贯穿整个接触过程。应预判接下来可能需要的照护，确认接收团队能力是否匹配，并解决不匹配之处。来源中的十五分钟间隔、一次正常生命体征或到达医院，都不代表交接已完成。整合照护还需明确角色、设备、监测和恶化时的应对；患者人数不是普遍适用的配员规则。

00:13:30.096 --> 00:14:03.048
Use ATMIST AMBO to transfer the clinical picture and SBAR to obtain a consultation recommendation. Make space for clarification without stopping lifesaving care. If someone declines an action, clarify the specific choice, understanding, risks and alternatives through the applicable framework; custody, distress or a diagnosis alone does not create coercion power. Record the actual discussion and accepted next responsibility, not a reassuring label or a signature alone.
使用ATMIST AMBO交接临床信息，以SBAR获取咨询建议。应允许澄清，同时不中断救命照护。若患者拒绝某项行动，应按适用框架说明具体选择，核对理解，并讨论风险与替代方案。羁押、情绪困扰或某个诊断，本身不赋予强制权。记录真实讨论及已被接受的后续责任，不能只写一个令人安心的标签或依赖签名。

00:14:03.048 --> 00:14:33.528
The PMHN section connects self-awareness with therapeutic communication and boundaries. Notice the urge to rush, rescue or defend yourself, then check it against the actual interaction. Explain before touching, use focused accessible questions and verify the response. A distressed person need not become emotionally neutral before urgent care. A professional relationship supports the patient; it does not ask them to carry the clinician's feelings.
PMHN把自我觉察与治疗性沟通、专业边界联系起来。察觉自己想催促、拯救或辩解的冲动，再根据实际互动核对。接触前先解释，提出聚焦且容易理解的问题，并确认回应。患者不必先恢复情绪平静，才有资格获得紧急照护。专业关系应支持患者，不能让患者承担临床人员的情绪。

00:14:33.528 --> 00:15:02.520
Use the reflection sequence to move from description and feelings to evaluation, analysis, conclusion and an action plan. Choose three observable priorities for the official self-assessment and later remediation. State the missed behavior, context, consequence, drill and how improvement will be checked. The original practice aid is not Appendix G or an instructor assessment, and confidence alone is not evidence that a safety gap closed.
按反思顺序，从描述与感受进入评价、分析、结论和行动计划。为正式自评及后续补救选择三项可观察的重点：遗漏了什么行为、当时情境与后果、怎样练习、如何核查改善。原创练习辅助不是Appendix G或教官评估；自信也不能证明安全缺口已经解决。

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:29.592
The practical-criteria reference is no longer just a title. The actual page eighty links a separate public grading document, and its full body and appendix have now been checked. The extra school pages still cannot be matched in the identified copy. Learn the observed-performance standard, but do not mistake this reference for the hidden EENT lab instructions, Appendix G or an official instructor score.
实操标准现在不再只有书名。真实第80页链接到独立公开评分文件，正文及附录已完整核读。但学校另列页码仍无法与该副本对应。应学习可观察表现标准，不把这份参考误作隐藏EENT实验说明、Appendix G或教师正式分数。

00:15:29.592 --> 00:15:57.048
The source starts at one hundred and deducts weighted deficiencies. Major, moderate and minor are not fixed prices for missing words: the patient, indication, severity and sequence matter, and individual rows differ. In our eye-exposure run, the useful question is what you actually recognized, did and checked. A calm voice and a normal final number cannot erase an avoidable delay or an omitted critical action.
来源从百分之百起分，按不足项加权扣分。严重、中等和轻微不是少说某个词的固定价目；患者、指征、严重度及顺序都重要，各行也不同。眼暴露演练真正要问的是：你识别了什么、做了什么、核验了什么。声音镇定和最后数值正常，都不能抹去可避免延误或关键行动遗漏。

00:15:57.048 --> 00:16:24.432
A simulated patient cannot reproduce every abnormal pulse, skin finding or level of consciousness. Demonstrate the relevant technique, describe what you assessed and clarify the scenario finding. Do not invent a normal observation to keep the sequence smooth. The public rubric distinguishes deciding that an intervention is needed from performing the technical skill, and it allows clinically justified differences in examination order.
模拟患者不能重现每个异常脉搏、肤色或意识状态。应展示相关方法、说明评估内容，再澄清情景发现，不能为了流程顺畅编正常值。公开标准区分“判断需要干预”与“完成该技术”，也允许有临床理由的检查顺序差异。

00:16:24.432 --> 00:16:55.056
Return to the child airway and the irrigated eye. An exhaustive throat examination can be the wrong action, and a complete adult score does not evaluate the local eye injury. Gather the evidence that changes care, act on the immediate threat, confirm the response and update transport priority. A technically tidy low-value task may still delay the action that matters. The reading shows every assessment domain without making every test compulsory in every case.
回到儿童气道及正在冲洗的眼睛：详查咽喉可能是错误行动，完整成人评分也不能评估局部眼伤。应取得会改变照护的证据，处理即时威胁、核反应并更新转运优先级。低价值操作即使做得整齐，仍可能拖延关键行动。阅读讲解各评估领域，但不把每项检查都变成所有情景的必做任务。

00:16:55.056 --> 00:17:23.208
The medication table and appendix must be read together. The document expects safe administration, while the appendix says that failing to recite the six-rights list itself does not attract a deduction. That never removes the actual checks. Likewise, the source pain examples compare eligible treatments and the consequences of delay. They are not instructions to give every patient three medicines or to ignore a contraindication.
给药表与附录必须一起读。文件要求安全给药，附录则说没有背出六项核对清单本身不扣分；这绝不取消实际核查。同样，源镇痛示例比较的是适用治疗和延误后果，不要求人人给三种药，也不允许忽略禁忌。

00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:51.312
In this station, first decide whether a medicine is indicated and authorized at all. Then verify the actual product, dose, route, equipment, relevant history and response. A correct volume is insufficient if the decision was wrong. If the step was entirely omitted, the source treats that differently from an observed technical error; the observer should record the real gap once, not invent several duplicate deductions.
在本站，先判断是否确实有药物指征及授权，再核真实产品、剂量途径、器材、相关病史和反应。决定错时，体积正确也不够。来源把完全漏做与已观察到的技术错误区分，观察者应准确记录实际缺口，而不是编出几项重复扣分。

00:17:51.312 --> 00:18:19.344
The rubric looks beyond the first successful action. Reassess the airway, breathing, circulation and primary interventions after important movement or change. A reassessment-delay example is not permission to wait until its boundary. In the eye station, confirm the care still works while the next task proceeds, and carry a persistent vision concern into the receiving plan even if routine observations look reassuring.
评分不只看第一次操作成功。重要移动或改变后，要复评气道、呼吸、循环及初始干预。复评延迟的扣分示例不是允许等到边界。眼站中，在进行下一任务时仍需确认照护有效；即使常规观察看似良好，也要把持续视力担忧带入接收计划。

00:18:19.344 --> 00:18:49.992
Give an organized notification and handover, then an accurate readable PCR. Use the five-minute exercise to select important facts, not to replace missing evidence. End the rehearsal with three observable priorities: what happened, why it mattered, the drill and what will prove improvement. This is original preparation for the school process, not a submitted form, an examination appeal or an assertion that reading alone proves practical competence.
需有组织地通知交接，再写准确可读PCR。五分钟练习用于选择重要事实，不是替换缺失证据。演练结束选三项可观察重点：发生了什么、为何重要、如何练及用什么证明改善。这是为学校流程做原创准备，不是提交表格、考试申诉，也不声称仅阅读便证明了实操能力。

00:18:49.992 --> 00:19:19.032
The actual cardiovascular chapter explains the rhythm mechanisms before its calcium and potassium sections. Use the same observation sequence for a new tracing: verify the patient and signal, assess perfusion, then describe atrial activity, ventricular activity, their relationship and the complex width. A rhythm label or a tall T wave does not give you a laboratory concentration, and a reassuring tracing does not erase a concerning patient history.
真实心血管章节先解释节律机制，再讲钙钾。新记录仍用同一顺序：核患者及信号、评灌注，再描述房室活动、相互关系及波群宽度。心律标签或高T波不能给出化验浓度，记录看似放心也不能抹去令人担忧的病史。

00:19:19.032 --> 00:19:47.280
A rapid irregular pattern, a blocked atrial impulse and a broad ventricular complex represent different questions. A hidden P wave is not automatically atrial fibrillation; a two-to-one block is not automatically Mobitz two; and a wide complex does not prove one cause. Explain the evidence that supports your interpretation and the information still missing instead of using one memorized feature as a treatment command.
快速不齐、心房冲动未下传及宽心室波群，是不同问题。看不见P不自动等于房颤，2:1阻滞不自动等于二度II型，宽波也不证明唯一病因。应解释支持判断的证据及缺失信息，不把一个背熟特征当成治疗命令。

00:19:47.280 --> 00:20:15.528
The calcium figure changes the recovery interval: higher calcium tends to shorten the plateau and ST or QT, while lower calcium tends to lengthen them. The low-potassium figures show altered recovery, a flattened T, prominent U and possible early extra depolarization. Learn what the drawing explains, but do not mistake a U for another atrial beat or use a J wave as a specific calcium or temperature test.
钙图改变的是恢复间隔：高钙倾向缩短平台期及ST或QT，低钙倾向延长。低钾图显示恢复改变、T低平、U明显及可能的早期额外除极。应学图示机制，但不能把U当另一次心房搏动，也不能把J波当特异的钙或体温检测。

00:20:15.528 --> 00:20:46.608
With high potassium, persistent membrane depolarization can eventually reduce available fast sodium channels and slow conduction. This helps connect a broad or unusual slow rhythm to the mechanism. The source illustrations are possible patterns, not a dependable laboratory staging sequence. Do not wait for every illustrated stage. Do not treat the overlapping source ranges as universal cutoffs. Do not assume that absent classic changes exclude danger.
高钾时，膜持续去极化最终可减少可用快速钠通道并减慢传导，有助于联系宽波或异常慢节律。源图是可能模式，不是可靠化验分期顺序。不能等每个图示阶段出现，不能把重叠源范围当通用界值，也不能因缺经典变化就排除危险。

00:20:46.608 --> 00:21:17.568
Extend our original eye rehearsal: necessary irrigation is underway, and the patient reports marked weakness and missed dialysis while the pulse seems unusually slow. Do not assume that the eye complaint explains everything. Allocate continuing eye care and a focused systemic assessment, verify the observation and identify the immediate breathing or perfusion problem. Electrolyte toxicity is a concern to communicate, not a concentration you have measured.
延伸原创眼站：必要冲洗已进行，患者诉明显无力及漏透析，脉搏似乎异常慢。不能假定眼部主诉解释一切。应分配持续眼护及聚焦全身评估，核观察并识即时呼吸或灌注问题。电解质毒性是需沟通的担忧，不是你已经测出的浓度。

00:21:17.568 --> 00:21:50.736
A source discussion of calcium, potassium or an advanced treatment does not expand your role. Continue indicated support, obtain appropriate help and use the actual authorized pathway. After a move or meaningful intervention, reassess the patient and treatment. Hand over both concerns with the real initial and latest findings, response and missing information. The useful reflection names a missed verification or communication behavior and a repeatable repair, not simply a confidence score.
来源讨论钙钾或高级治疗，不会扩大你的角色。应继续有指征支持、求适当帮助并循真实授权路径。移动或重要干预后，要复评患者及治疗。交接应包括两个问题、真实初始及最新发现、反应和缺失信息。有效反思应指出漏核查或沟通行为及可重复修复，而不只是自信分数。

00:21:50.736 --> 00:22:19.776
The CNS reading joins nursing principles, evidence and a care process. Keep its frameworks distinct. Tanner describes noticing, interpreting, responding and reflecting. ADPIE organizes a care plan. The model author's actual six measurable judgment processes differ from the Chapter one box, so the reading shows the correction explicitly. None of these frameworks replaces an urgent patient response or expands your role.
CNS阅读把护理原则、证据和照护过程联系起来，但要分清框架。Tanner描述注意、解释、响应及反思，ADPIE组织照护计划。模型作者真实六项可测判断过程，与第1章框内不同，阅读已明确纠正。任何框架都不替代紧急患者响应，也不扩大角色。

00:22:19.776 --> 00:22:47.232
Apply the framework to the same eye and systemic-risk encounter. Say what you noticed, why it matters, which alternative remains possible and what authorized action follows. Then identify the response you will check. A filled form, a spoken acronym or a confident explanation cannot stand in for a treatment that never happened, an unreliable measurement or an unverified delegated task.
把框架用于同一眼部及全身风险接触：说出注意到什么、为何重要、仍有什么替代解释，以及接下来何种获授权行动，再指出如何核反应。表格填满、说出缩写或解释自信，都不能代替没有发生的治疗、不可靠测量或未核验委派。

00:22:47.232 --> 00:23:16.680
Evidence-based practice is not choosing the newest paper or the highest box in a pyramid. Ask a relevant question, find the evidence, appraise its quality and fit, apply it through the proper process and assess the result. A correlation does not prove causation, and a research design name does not guarantee quality. The assigned reading explains the article sections, quantitative and qualitative approaches and the two evidence diagrams.
循证实践不是挑最新论文或金字塔最高一格。应提相关问题、找证据、评质量及适用性，经适当流程应用并评结果。相关不证明因果，设计名称不保证质量。指定阅读解释论文各部分、定量定性方法及两幅证据图。

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:45.840
The person's values and resources belong in that decision. Ask rather than assume what a family, age group or cultural label means. Theory can help you notice needs, but it does not assign capacity or a treatment preference. Preserve permission, privacy and honest communication while necessary care continues. A plan that requires unavailable resources or ignores the patient's priorities may be tidy on paper and unusable in practice.
患者价值及资源也属于决定。应询问，不凭家庭、年龄或文化标签推定含义。理论有助于识需要，却不判定能力或治疗意愿。必要照护进行时，仍需许可、隐私及诚实沟通。依赖不可得资源或忽略患者重点的计划，可能纸上整齐、实际不可用。

00:23:45.840 --> 00:24:13.704
Build a short plan rather than copying a nursing form. Link the priority concern to a measurable patient result, the real action, the responsible person and a reassessment trigger. An outcome is not merely a task such as applying equipment. It describes what you need to observe afterward. If the person cannot participate in teach-back or the task would delay urgent care, choose an appropriate accessible alternative and preserve the immediate priority.
应建立简短计划，不是抄护理表。把优先担忧连到可测患者结果、真实行动、负责人及复评触发。结果不只是戴设备等任务，而是之后需要看到什么。若患者不能复述或任务会拖延急护，应选适当可及替代方式，并保即时优先级。

00:24:13.704 --> 00:24:43.008
Implementation and evaluation stay connected. Record what was actually done, verify the patient and the delegated work, compare the new findings with the intended response and revise when necessary. One improved number does not settle every remaining concern. A completed goal does not release care responsibility without an accepted transition. Carry both the eye complaint and the persistent systemic risk into a truthful handover and PCR.
实施及评价需相连。记录实际行动，核患者及委派工作，将新发现与预期反应比较，必要时修订。一个数字改善不解决所有剩余担忧，目标达成也不在没有已接受转接时解除责任。真实交接及PCR需同时保眼部主诉与持续全身风险。

00:24:43.008 --> 00:25:16.440
The assigned case illustrates recognizing needs, refining interventions and evaluating outcomes, but its hospital examples are not field orders. Do not turn a worried appearance into an anxiety diagnosis. Do not use a sedative merely to slow breathing. Do not copy a routine observation interval for an unstable person. Verify the measurement while indicated support continues and use the actual patient-specific pathway. Later education also needs verified data and a feasible individual plan.
指定案例说明识需要、修订干预及评结果，但住院示例不是现场医嘱。不能因外观担忧就诊断焦虑，不能仅为降低呼吸次数给镇静药，也不能把常规观察间隔抄给不稳定者。需在有指征支持持续时核测量，并循真实个体化路径。之后教育也需可靠数据及可行个人计划。

00:25:16.440 --> 00:25:47.448
End our original rehearsal by identifying three behaviors that could improve. Name the missed cue, delay, verification or communication; explain its consequence; choose a repeatable drill and how an observer will check it next time. This applies the reading without reproducing the textbook patient's answers or inventing an instructor score. Practical competence still requires the school's actual demonstration and feedback, not a count of completed paragraphs.
原创排练结束时应找三项可改善行为。指出漏线索、延迟、核验或沟通问题，解释后果、选择可重复练法，并说明观察者下次怎样核。这把阅读用于实践，却不复制教材患者答案或编教师分数。实操能力仍需学校真实展示及反馈，不由完成段落数量证明。

00:25:47.448 --> 00:26:16.944
The FON review carries the care process from assessment to documentation. It adds a useful quality distinction to our current case. Available equipment and trained people describe resources; the actual action describes a process; the patient's response describes an outcome. One does not prove the next. A stocked irrigation supply does not establish effective eye care, and one improved observation does not settle the persistent systemic concern.
FON复习把照护过程从评估带到记录，并为当前案例加入有用质量区别。现有设备及受训人员描述资源，真实行动描述过程，患者反应描述结果。前者不证明后者。有冲洗物资不证明眼护有效，一个观察改善也不解决持续全身担忧。

00:26:16.944 --> 00:26:44.232
Use the distinction during debrief. If a task was missed, ask whether the problem was an absent resource, an unclear decision, a technical error or a failure to evaluate the result. Different failures need different repairs. Do not label a favorable outcome proof of perfect care, or a difficult outcome proof that every action was wrong. Compare actual evidence with the intended patient-centered plan.
复盘可用这个区别。任务漏做时，要问是缺资源、决定不清、技术错误，还是未评价结果；不同失败需不同修复。不能把好结果当完美照护证明，也不能因结果困难便判每个行动都错。需用真实证据对照预期的以患者为中心计划。

00:26:44.232 --> 00:27:15.552
The reading compares narrative notes and structured methods such as SOAP, PIE and focus documentation. Their useful common feature is a traceable chain from finding to interpretation, action and response. They are not instructions to submit several duplicate nursing charts. Use the actual required PCR and preserve the relevant source, time, patient finding, real intervention and reassessment. A prepared dose or planned task must not be recorded as completed care.
阅读比较叙述记录及SOAP、PIE、焦点记录等结构方法，共同有用之处是能从发现追到解释、行动及反应。它们不要求提交几份重复护理表。应使用真实要求的PCR，保相关来源、时间、患者发现、真实干预及复评。备好剂量或计划任务不能记成已完成照护。

00:27:15.552 --> 00:27:46.488
Finish the eye and systemic-risk encounter with an accepted handover, not merely a finished document. Carry forward what remains uncertain, what needs continued care and who has the next responsibility. Then select the three practice priorities using the observed assessment, decision, implementation or evaluation gap. This is preparation for the school process, not a fabricated form, signature, score or proof that reading alone establishes practical competence.
眼部及全身风险接触应以已接受交接结束，不只是文件写完。需传递未定内容、持续照护需要及下一责任人，再按可见评估、决定、实施或评价缺口选三练习重点。这是学校流程准备，不是伪造表格、签名或分数，也不证明只读便具实操能力。

00:27:46.488 --> 00:28:19.344
The nursing assignment reviews management across fifteen chapters. Start with a clinical problem, then explain the mechanism, expected findings, useful investigation and purpose of treatment. Finally describe how to recognize benefit or harm. Our bilingual reader supplies the detailed chapters; this connected rehearsal tests whether those ideas change a decision. The chapter count is a navigation aid, not a claim that knowing a diagnosis name makes you ready for an independent school scenario.
学校指定复习横跨十五章的护理管理内容。应从临床问题出发，解释机制、预期发现、有用检查和治疗目的，再说明如何识别获益或伤害。详细章节讲解在双语读本中；这里的连贯排练检验这些知识是否真正改变决策。章节数量只是导航，知道诊断名称并不代表已能独立完成学校情景。

00:28:19.344 --> 00:28:51.888
Separate the visible problem from the whole patient. In our established eye exposure encounter, suitable eye care must continue, but new breathlessness, weakness or confusion needs its own assessment. Do not invent a hidden diagnosis to explain those findings. Use actual history, timing, medicines and repeated observations to distinguish possibilities. Nursing investigations and hospital therapies tell you what the next team may consider, not what you may independently prescribe in the field.
把眼前局部问题与整体患者区分开。在既有眼部暴露案例中，适当眼部照护应继续，但新出现的呼吸困难、无力或意识混乱需要另外评估。不要编造隐含诊断来解释这些发现。应结合真实病史、时间、用药和重复观察，比较可能病因。护理教材中的院内检查与治疗用于理解后续照护，不授权在现场自行开立治疗。

00:28:51.888 --> 00:29:24.792
Consider a separate rehearsal branch: the patient reports vomiting and poor intake before the exposure, but has no laboratory results available. Reduced circulating volume is possible; sodium, potassium and acid-base abnormalities cannot be named from that history alone. Look for competing causes and assess the trend. Chapter ten explains the relationships; cardiac and shock chapters explain why the same fluid quantity is not an automatic answer for every weak or hypotensive patient.
考虑另一个排练分支：患者报告暴露前有呕吐、进食饮水不足，但目前没有化验结果。循环血容量减少是一种可能，却不能仅凭这段病史就诊断钠、钾或酸碱异常。应寻找竞争病因并评估趋势。第十章解释这些关系，心脏与休克章节则说明：同样的液体量并不是所有无力或低血压患者的通用答案。

00:29:24.792 --> 00:30:00.888
Blood lost into the chest or abdomen is real loss even when it is not visible. By contrast, vasodilation or permeability can change useful distribution without the same external loss. Pump failure and obstructed return require different reasoning again, and mechanisms may coexist. Control a treatable source, follow the applicable authorized pathway and look for both intended improvement and respiratory deterioration. A pressure increase or more urine does not independently prove that tissue oxygen delivery is now sufficient.
出血进入胸腔或腹腔，即使外表看不到，仍是真实的血液丢失。血管扩张或通透性增加则可能在没有同等外部丢失时，改变有效血液分布。泵功能衰竭、回流受阻又需要不同推理，且多种机制可以并存。控制可处理的原因，遵循适用的获授权路径，同时观察预期改善及呼吸恶化。血压升高或尿量增加，均不能单独证明组织供氧已充足。

00:30:00.888 --> 00:30:33.024
Keep the actual child in our upper-airway case distinct from an adult allergy branch. Drooling, distress and a threatened upper airway are not permission for a forced throat examination. A wheeze describes a finding, not its cause; asthma, infection and systemic allergic disease are different possibilities in the appropriate context. Explain where airflow may be threatened, which observations are safe and what immediate support or escalation is required before discussing a full differential.
应把既有儿童上气道案例，与成人过敏分支分清。流涎、呼吸窘迫和上气道受威胁，并不允许强行检查咽喉。哮鸣音描述的是发现，而非病因；在相应情境下，哮喘、感染和全身过敏反应是不同可能。先解释气流可能在哪一环受威胁、哪些观察安全、需要什么即时支持或升级，再展开完整鉴别。

00:30:33.024 --> 00:31:09.072
In the allergy branch, rapid tongue swelling with breathing or circulatory compromise calls for anaphylaxis assessment without waiting for hives, an immunoglobulin E result or imaging. Initial epinephrine uses the current intramuscular pathway, not the subcutaneous route printed in the nursing chapter. An antihistamine, steroid or inhaled treatment must not take its place. Reassess deeper airway swelling and perfusion even when the skin looks better; possible bradykinin swelling also requires early airway planning and cause-specific help.
过敏分支中，快速出现的舌部肿胀伴呼吸或循环受损，需要立即评估过敏性反应，不等待风团、免疫球蛋白E（IgE）结果或影像。初始肾上腺素遵循现行肌注路径，不采用护理教材的皮下途径。抗组胺药、激素或吸入治疗不能替代它。即使皮肤表现改善，仍须复评深部气道肿胀及灌注；可能的缓激肽性肿胀也需要早期气道计划及针对病因的援助。

00:31:09.072 --> 00:31:41.592
A new confused answer is not automatically a local eye problem, a stroke or a glucose disorder. Determine onset and baseline, assess relevant neurological function, check glucose through the actual procedure and review perfusion, breathing, medicines and seizure history. One explanation does not eliminate another. A normal-looking pupil, a corrected glucose or a temporarily clearer answer cannot independently cancel a credible new focal deficit or a deteriorating trajectory.
新出现的意识混乱，不能自动归因于局部眼病、卒中或血糖异常。确定起始时间和基线，评估相关神经功能，按实际程序测血糖，并核查灌注、呼吸、用药和癫痫发作史。一种解释不能排除另一种。瞳孔看似正常、血糖纠正或暂时回答更清楚，都不能独自否定可信的新局灶缺损或恶化趋势。

00:31:41.592 --> 00:32:17.808
The endocrine reader separates chronic diagnosis from an emergency. An A one c result is not the same information as current glucose, and diabetes insipidus is not glucose-driven diuresis. Thyroid, adrenal and water-balance disorders have different pathways, risks and prescribed plans. Use that knowledge to ask useful questions and communicate uncertainty. Do not independently stop prescribed steroids. Do not independently select a sodium-correction rate. Do not treat one hormone result as a complete diagnosis.
内分泌读本区分慢性病诊断与急症。A1c结果提供的信息不同于当前血糖，尿崩症也不是葡萄糖引起的渗透性利尿。甲状腺、肾上腺及水平衡疾病有不同通路、风险和处方计划。利用这些知识提出有用的问题，并传达不确定性。不要自行停用处方激素，不要自行选择纠正血钠的速度，也不要把一个激素结果当作完整诊断。

00:32:17.808 --> 00:32:50.616
Suppose an additional practice branch includes a wound and pain after a fall. Describe the actual skin injury, deformity, distal function and circulation without forcing movement to prove the anatomy. A small surface wound does not measure deep damage, and worsening pain or neurovascular change needs reassessment. The skin and musculoskeletal chapters link injury, healing, infection risk and longer-term function; they do not turn a photograph or a nursing device paragraph into your procedure instruction.
假设新增练习分支为跌倒后的伤口和疼痛。描述真实皮肤损伤、畸形、远端功能及循环，不能靠强行活动来证明解剖判断。表面伤口小，不能说明深部损伤小；疼痛加重或神经血管改变需要复评。皮肤和肌骨章节把损伤、愈合、感染风险与长期功能相连，但照片或护理设备段落本身不是个人操作指令。

00:32:50.616 --> 00:33:24.000
Ask about an antiplatelet, anticoagulant, bleeding history or blood disorder without assuming every drug has the same reversal. Platelet problems and coagulation-factor problems can produce different patterns, while disseminated coagulation can combine clotting and bleeding. Blood components have distinct functions and risks. Explain what is actually bleeding, what suggests impaired perfusion and what has changed after permitted measures; a laboratory number or transfusion product name alone is not a treatment plan.
询问抗血小板药、抗凝药、出血史及血液病史，不能假设所有药物都有同样的逆转方法。血小板问题与凝血因子问题可有不同表现，弥散性凝血异常则可能同时出现血栓与出血。不同血液成分具有不同功能和风险。解释实际哪里在出血、哪些发现提示灌注不足，以及获准措施后有何变化；一个化验数字或血制品名称不能构成治疗计划。

00:33:24.000 --> 00:34:03.216
Abdominal symptoms can arise from several organs or a systemic problem. Compare vomiting, distension, stool, bleeding, oral intake and urine change with actual examination and baseline. Obstruction and ileus are not identical, chronic irritable bowel symptoms do not explain every new severe pain, and jaundice does not identify a hepatitis virus. Gastrointestinal and genitourinary chapters teach investigation and hospital treatment purposes; field care still prioritizes threats, useful history, support and an appropriate destination.
腹部症状可来自多个器官，也可来自全身问题。应把呕吐、腹胀、大便、出血、摄入及尿液变化，与真实检查和基线比较。肠梗阻与肠麻痹不同；慢性肠易激症状不能解释所有新发剧烈腹痛；黄疸也不能确定是哪一种肝炎病毒。胃肠与泌尿章节解释检查及院内治疗目的，现场仍优先处理威胁、取得有用病史、提供支持并选择适当目的地。

00:34:03.216 --> 00:34:41.856
Renal impairment changes fluid tolerance, drug handling and electrolyte risk. High potassium can affect cardiac conduction, yet a reassuring tracing cannot exclude it. Calcium can protect the myocardium in selected treatment but does not itself remove potassium; moving potassium into cells is also different from eliminating it. Those mechanisms explain why hospital therapies are not interchangeable. Keep the actual dialysis and access history, medicines and current observations in the handover, without inventing a potassium value or bypassing the authorized care pathway.
肾功能受损会改变液体耐受、药物处理和电解质风险。高钾可影响心脏传导，但看似正常的心电图不能排除高钾。某些治疗中，钙用于保护心肌，却不直接移除钾；把钾移入细胞，也不同于把钾排出体外。这解释了不同院内治疗为何不能互换。交接真实透析及通路病史、用药和当前观察，不能编造血钾数值或绕过获授权的照护路径。

00:34:41.856 --> 00:35:14.784
In an original infection branch, a patient has new weakness, faster breathing and a recent illness, without a dramatic fever. Consider serious infection alongside other causes; a normal screening score or one negative test does not erase actual deterioration. Protect the scene and use appropriate precautions while supporting breathing and perfusion. Identify a possible source and notify the receiving team. The task is not to finish naming every cytokine before time-sensitive treatment begins.
原创感染分支中，患者新出现无力、呼吸加快及近期患病史，但没有明显高热。应同时考虑严重感染及其他病因；正常筛查评分或一次阴性检测，不能抹去真实恶化。在保护现场、采取适当防护的同时，支持呼吸和灌注，寻找可能感染源，并通知接收团队。不能等说完所有细胞因子，才开始时间敏感的治疗。

00:35:14.784 --> 00:35:52.608
The infection chapter also changes communication. HIV monitoring is not diagnosis by a low white-cell count; a positive resistance screen is not automatically active infection; and diarrheal odor does not diagnose C difficile. Appropriate treatment route matters: intravenous vancomycin is not equivalent to bowel-lumen delivery. Report symptoms, exposure, actual tests, devices and medicines accurately. Avoid stigma and unnecessary assumptions while preserving the precautions, urgent care and specialist decisions that the real findings require.
感染章节也影响交接内容。白细胞低不是HIV诊断；耐药菌筛查阳性不自动等于活动性感染；腹泻气味不能诊断艰难梭菌感染。给药途径有意义，静脉万古霉素不等于把药物送入肠腔。准确报告症状、暴露、真实检测、器械和用药，避免污名与无根据假设，同时保留实际发现所要求的防护、紧急照护和专科决策。

00:35:52.608 --> 00:36:29.208
For a final separate trauma branch, imagine new weakness after injury with low pressure and a slow pulse. Neurogenic physiology is possible, but it cannot excuse ignoring hidden bleeding or impaired ventilation. Distinguish circulatory neurogenic shock from neurological spinal shock. A hospital mean-pressure target and a BC field systolic target are not interchangeable numbers. State the real observations, supported possibilities and permitted next actions rather than reciting a textbook label as if it had settled the whole encounter.
最后考虑独立创伤分支：损伤后出现无力、低血压和慢脉。神经源性机制是一种可能，却不能据此忽略隐匿出血或通气不足。应区分循环方面的神经源性休克，与神经功能方面的脊髓休克。院内平均动脉压目标与BC现场收缩压目标不能互换。说明真实观察、有依据的可能及获准下一步，不能靠背出病名就宣称整个接触已解释清楚。

00:36:29.208 --> 00:37:02.832
Now teach back one complete branch: what you noticed, what it might mean, what else remains possible, what you did and what changed. Include the treatment purpose, a serious adverse effect to watch for and the unresolved concern handed over. Use the fifteen chapter rounds to repair gaps in that chain, then demonstrate the relevant school skill with an observer. The narrated review prepares independent work; it cannot invent the school result, replace deliberate practice or certify competence from a paragraph count.
现在用自己的话讲完整分支：注意到什么、可能意味着什么、还有什么可能、实际做了什么、之后改变了什么。包括治疗目的、需警惕的严重不良作用，以及交接中仍未解决的担忧。用十五章阅读补齐推理链中的缺口，再由观察者见证相关学校技能。配音复习用于准备独立工作，不代替刻意练习，不编造学校结果，也不以段落数量认证能力。

00:37:02.832 --> 00:37:31.704
The school asks for review of all twenty-eight A and P chapters. We will not turn that into hundreds of isolated micro-lessons. The bilingual reader supplies the full chapter-by-chapter explanations; these pages show how to use them in our existing eye and airway encounters. Start with organization: a tissue finding reflects cells, membranes, blood supply and coordinated systems, not just an organ label.
学校要求复习A&P全部28章。我们不把它变成几百节孤立微课，双语读本提供逐章完整讲解，这几页示范怎样用于既有眼部及气道接触。先从组织层次起：组织发现反映细胞、膜、供血及协调系统，不只是器官标签。

00:37:31.704 --> 00:38:01.968
Follow the mechanism behind an observation. Sodium and potassium gradients support excitability; transport and repair need energy. Production of adenosine triphosphate needs usable fuel and functioning pathways as well as delivery. A normal-looking number cannot establish all those links. Use the early chapters to explain what the measurement represents, what it misses and which new observation could test your concern while indicated care continues.
追踪观察结果背后的机制：钠、钾梯度支持兴奋性，运输和修复需要能量。三磷酸腺苷（ATP）的生成不仅需要物质输送，还需要可用的燃料和正常的代谢路径。一个貌似正常的数值不能证明所有环节都正常。用前几章的知识解释测量代表什么、遗漏什么，以及哪项新观察有助于检验当前担忧，同时继续提供有指征的照护。

00:38:01.968 --> 00:38:30.960
Skin, connective tissue, skeleton, joints and muscles solve different parts of protection and movement. In a splash exposure, a barrier failure is not the same as a muscle or bone injury. In a possible penetrating eye injury, tissue structure explains why pressure or forced manipulation can add harm. The reader separates regional anatomy, joint motion and muscle action so that a familiar movement name does not replace protection of the actual patient.
皮肤、结缔组织、骨骼、关节及肌肉，在保护和运动中承担不同任务。化学溅洒造成的屏障损伤，不同于肌肉或骨损伤。疑似眼穿透伤时，组织结构解释了为何施压或强行操作可能增加伤害。读本区分区域解剖、关节运动和肌肉作用，避免用一个熟悉的动作名称替代对真实患者的保护。

00:38:30.960 --> 00:39:03.312
A muscle action requires a coordinated chain: neural activation, junctional transmission, calcium-linked force, energy and an appropriate mechanical attachment. Failure at one link can reduce movement without proving unwillingness. Do not force range, strength or a painful eye movement merely to complete a checklist. Compare the relevant observation with history, sensory findings and function, and use the actual school examination method when the test is appropriate.
肌肉动作依赖完整协同链：神经激活、接头传递、钙参与产力、能量供应及适当的机械附着。任何环节失效都可能减少运动，不能直接认定患者不愿配合。不要只为完成清单而强测活动范围、肌力或有疼痛的眼球运动。结合病史、感觉发现和功能比较，只有适合检查时，才使用学校的实际检查方法。

00:39:03.312 --> 00:39:36.648
For an eye finding, separate the receptor and optical route from neural interpretation and the motor response. Retina and visual pathways support seeing; eye-movement circuits position the globe; pupil-light circuitry regulates aperture. A visible pupil response does not establish normal visual acuity or exclude injury elsewhere. Cranial nerve two provides visual afferent input and nerve three contributes pupil motor output, but one pupil observation is not a complete neurological examination.
分析眼部发现时，区分感光受体与光学路径、神经解释及运动反应。视网膜和视觉通路支持视物；眼球运动回路控制位置；瞳孔光反射调节孔径。能看到瞳孔反应，不代表视力正常，也不能排除其他部位损伤。第二脑神经提供视觉传入，第三脑神经参与瞳孔运动输出，但一次瞳孔观察不是完整神经检查。

00:39:36.648 --> 00:40:09.600
The neuro chapters also explain why awareness, language, attention, sensation and strength can dissociate. Use the appropriate safe comparison rather than assuming that a confused answer proves a local eye problem or that normal movement clears every central concern. Document what was actually tested and what prevented a valid test. The detailed receptor, pathway, autonomic and examination rounds are available together in the reader; they are not a list of diagnoses inferred from one sign.
神经章节也解释了意识、语言、注意、感觉和肌力为何可能分别受损。应进行适当且安全的比较，不能因回答混乱就认定是局部眼病，也不能凭运动正常排除所有中枢问题。记录实际检查项目，以及什么因素妨碍了有效检查。读本把受体、通路、自主神经和检查方法连在一起，不是供人凭单一体征推断诊断的清单。

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:41.712
Return to the adult whose eye care must continue while a systemic concern remains. Hormone history can change glucose and water handling; blood carries oxygen; the heart generates flow and vessels distribute it. None is certified by a normal oxygen saturation alone. A displayed electrical rhythm is not measured cardiac output. Relate the current mental status, breathing and perfusion findings to the whole delivery chain rather than assigning every symptom to the visible eye exposure.
回到成人案例：眼部照护必须继续，但全身担忧仍未解决。激素相关病史会影响葡萄糖和水的处理；血液携氧，心脏产生血流，血管分配血流。正常血氧饱和度不能证明这些环节全部正常，显示出的电节律也不是实测心排血量。应把意识、呼吸及灌注发现连到整个输送链，不能把每个症状都归于可见的眼部暴露。

00:40:41.712 --> 00:41:14.400
Immune and lymphatic chapters add defense, fluid return and the possibility of harmful responses. Inflammation is not always infection; a local reaction is not automatically systemic anaphylaxis or sepsis; immunosuppression can change the expected signs. Ask for the history that matters and follow the actual assessment pathway. Do not delay an immediate threat while naming every mediator, and do not use a textbook hormone or immune label as an unassigned medication order.
免疫与淋巴章节补充防御、液体回流和有害反应。炎症不一定是感染，局部反应不自动等于全身过敏反应或脓毒症，免疫抑制还可能改变预期体征。询问相关病史并遵循实际评估路径。不能为了说完每种介质而延误即时威胁，也不能把教材中的激素或免疫名词当成未获授权的给药指令。

00:41:14.400 --> 00:41:45.864
Use an original arithmetic rehearsal, not a ventilation prescription. Assume one hundred and fifty millilitres of dead space per breath. Three hundred and fifty millilitres at eighteen breaths per minute and two hundred and ten at thirty both give six point three litres per minute total. Subtract dead space before multiplying: the estimated alveolar amounts are three point six and one point eight litres per minute. A faster rate has not preserved effective ventilation in this assumed model.
进行原创算术练习，而非设定通气处方。假设每次呼吸死腔为150毫升：潮气量350毫升、每分钟18次，与210毫升、每分钟30次，分钟通气总量都为6.3升。先从每次潮气量减去死腔再乘频率，估计肺泡通气量分别为每分钟3.6升和1.8升。这个假设模型说明：频率增加并没有维持同样的有效通气。

00:41:45.864 --> 00:42:21.192
Respiratory exchange, blood carriage and cellular metabolism then remain separate links. Digestive chapters explain how nutrients reach blood or lymph; metabolic chapters explain how cells use them to make adenosine triphosphate, store fuel and produce heat. Glucose availability, ketone use and mitochondrial function are not read directly from the saturation display. In the tiring child or adult, use the mechanism to recognize what needs assessment and support, not to finish a biochemistry calculation before responding.
呼吸交换、血液运输和细胞代谢仍是不同环节。消化章节解释营养物质怎样进入血液或淋巴，代谢章节解释细胞怎样利用它们生成三磷酸腺苷（ATP）、储存燃料和产生热量。葡萄糖是否可用、酮体利用及线粒体功能，都不能直接从血氧饱和度显示中读出。儿童或成人出现疲乏时，应利用这些机制识别需要评估和支持的环节，而不是先完成生化计算才作出响应。

00:42:21.192 --> 00:42:53.256
The kidney filters a large load and recovers most of it; final urine reflects both filtration and tubular regulation. Water-retaining ADH and aldosterone, which affects sodium and potassium handling, act through different mechanisms. Swelling does not prove useful circulating volume, and a sodium concentration does not count all body sodium. Ask about actual renal history, medicines, recent losses and urine change rather than inventing findings for the eye-exposure case.
肾脏滤过大量物质并回收其中大部分，最终尿液同时反映滤过和肾小管调节。促进保水的抗利尿激素（ADH），与影响钠、钾处理的醛固酮，作用机制并不相同。水肿不能证明有效循环血量充足，血钠浓度也不等于全身钠总量。应询问真实的肾脏病史、用药、近期体液丢失和尿液变化，而不是为眼部暴露案例虚构这些发现。

00:42:53.256 --> 00:43:30.696
Read acid-base values as a relationship. In an assumed arterial example, pH seven point three eight, carbon dioxide fifty millimetres of mercury and bicarbonate twenty-nine millimoles per litre are not three normal results just because pH is within its familiar interval. Compensation, chronic adaptation or mixed processes need context. This pattern does not by itself choose the cause or treatment. The patient, sample, ventilation and trend remain essential, and a normal pH is not proof that a prior problem is cured.
酸碱指标要结合起来解释。假定动脉样本pH为7.38，二氧化碳分压50毫米汞柱，碳酸氢盐29毫摩尔每升；不能因为pH处于熟悉范围，就说三个结果都正常。补偿、慢性适应或混合过程都需要情境判断，这个组合本身不能确定病因或治疗。患者表现、样本性质、通气和趋势仍然关键；正常pH不证明原有问题已经治愈。

00:43:30.696 --> 00:44:04.032
Our existing cases include a child and an adult; do not silently turn either into a different patient. The reproductive and development review prepares additional contexts when actually relevant: pregnancy possibility, recent birth, age and neonatal transition. Ask respectfully without inferring organs or history from appearance. Pregnancy changes circulating and respiratory demands, but it does not make severe breathlessness, bleeding, syncope or neurological change automatically normal.
既有案例是一名儿童和一名成人，不能暗中把他们改成其他患者。生殖与发育复习帮助准备实际相关的额外情境，包括可能妊娠、近期分娩、年龄及新生儿转变。应尊重询问，不能从外观推断器官或病史。妊娠会改变循环和呼吸需求，但不会让严重气促、出血、晕厥或神经改变自动变正常。

00:44:04.032 --> 00:44:37.392
Before birth the placenta supports gas exchange; after birth lung aeration and circulatory transition must occur, while warmth and effective feeding matter. Functional shunt changes are not instantaneous permanent anatomical closure. Genetics and lactation chapters explain mechanisms, not a family prediction or a fixed feeding timer. Keep the current school newborn sequence separate from dated textbook suction or first-breath statements, and use the detailed bilingual rounds when revising these stages.
出生前由胎盘支持气体交换；出生后必须完成肺充气及循环转变，同时注意保暖和有效喂养。分流在功能上改变，不等于解剖结构瞬间永久闭合。遗传与哺乳章节解释机制，不预测特定家庭结果，也不规定固定喂养计时。应把学校现行新生儿流程，与旧教材的吸引或首口呼吸说法分开，复习这些阶段时使用详细双语阅读。

00:44:37.392 --> 00:45:06.576
Close the cumulative review by teaching back one observation from our real practice sequence. Explain the structure, signal or flow it represents; name an alternative explanation and the next useful observation. Then justify the permitted action and how you will judge its effect. You do not need to recite twenty-eight chapter titles while urgent care waits. You do need a defensible chain that survives reassessment and an accepted handover.
累计复习结束时，从实际练习顺序中挑一项观察，用自己的话解释它反映的结构、信号或血流，提出另一个可能解释及下一项有用观察，再说明获准行动与评价效果的方法。不能让紧急照护等待背完二十八个章名；需要的是经得起复评、并能传入已被接受交接中的推理链。

00:45:06.576 --> 00:45:37.536
Use chapter navigation to repair a specific knowledge gap, not a paragraph counter as proof of readiness. The reader preserves source errors, model assumptions and page boundaries so you can distinguish physiology from current clinical instructions. Demonstrate the school examination and practical behaviors with an observer, record what actually happened and select a repeatable repair. Reading and narration prepare that work; they do not fabricate the school score or complete its assessment for you.
利用章节导航修补具体知识缺口，不能把读完多少段当作准备度证明。读本保留来源错误、模型假设和页码界限，帮助区分生理解释与现行临床指令。向观察者展示学校要求的检查及实训行为，记录真实经过，再选择可重复的改进练习。阅读和配音为这些工作做准备，不伪造学校分数，也不代为完成考核。

00:45:37.536 --> 00:45:54.168
In the child case, do not spend time proving epiglottitis against an abscess. The defensible conclusion is a potentially critical upper-airway problem; keep the child calm and upright, avoid an oropharyngeal examination, and convey early.
儿童案例中，不要花时间试图证明是会厌炎还是脓肿。可支持的结论是“可能存在危重上气道问题”；让孩子安静并保持直立，避免检查口咽，及早转运。

00:45:54.168 --> 00:46:12.456
In the eye case, first prevent responder contamination and start suitable irrigation. The product label and consultation refine the plan while irrigation continues. In both cases, reassessment and handover are part of treatment—not paperwork added after the clinical work.
眼部案例中，先防止救援人员受污染并开始适当冲洗。冲洗继续进行时，再由产品标签和咨询意见细化计划。两个案例都必须把复评和交接视为治疗的一部分，而不是临床工作完成后的附加文书。

00:46:12.456 --> 00:46:30.936
For the pediatric airway, do not force an exam; for chemical eye exposure, do not delay suitable irrigation; for a penetrating eye injury, do not apply pressure; for epistaxis, lean forward and maintain pressure. These are distinct problems with different first actions.
儿童上气道问题不要强行检查；化学溅眼不要延误适当冲洗；眼穿透伤不要施压；鼻出血要前倾并持续按压。这些是不同问题，首要行动也不同。

00:46:30.936 --> 00:46:49.536
Read A01–A04 and the assigned exam source directly. Use this original lesson as an organized explanation and practice scaffold, not a substitute for school materials, current pathways, supervised lab instruction or final professional authorization.
直接阅读A01–A04和指定考试资料。本原创课程用于梳理解释和练习，不替代学校材料、现行流程、受监督的实验教学或最终执业授权。
